contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/test_insurance_recommendations.py","size":4799,"sha256":"d404cd264449ca30394ce7d9333d882dfa2fce748f8c6130626b10e216dfa9f8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/test_report_exporter.py","size":6890,"sha256":"1b7722bf8234afbc702e73c69df0a7a725a69236cbe8c2d420badb5c159b0771","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1871,"sha256":"5491d56b2849e79e4254635380b1ed720cc554c1b14135e8e2fa1e062f8f1394","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1792432436584,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"bf05a452f657199b1c0228e4ad868d1dc6cce70190fef4e5e7624d69f86764ec","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/bf05a452f657199b1c0228e4ad868d1dc6cce70190fef4e5e7624d69f86764ec","scanners":{"vt":null,"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":40,"checkedAt":1792432436584},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This career-planning skill is mostly disclosed and controlled, but its insurance recommendation module needs review because it embeds a declared business-priority recommendation and marks some mismatched insurance data as verified.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Local reference reads and optional report export fit the stated purpose; optional Tavily, AgentMail, agent-reach, and memory use are disclosed as user-triggered only.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No installer, dependency installation, tool wrapping, persistence hook, or automatic startup behavior was found; the frontmatter publication date is one day after the review date.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill asks for ordinary career-planning profile data and says to collect it progressively, but its activation wording is broad and one instruction suppresses civil-service recommendations unless the user asks.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The default behavior is offline and non-persistent; report writing is limited to an exports directory and tracking/memory instructions say not to write without explicit user request.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The core career-planning purpose is coherent, but the insurance onboarding branch prioritizes one company as a maintained business decision and the insurance dataset contains records marked verified even where snippets and sources describe unrelated entities.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review the insurance-company recommendation behavior before installing. The core career-planning workflow is offline and proportionate, but insurance suggestions should be treated as advisory and independently verified, especially records labeled verified and the built-in priority recommendation for one company.","findings":"[AE1] expected: The referenced salary_database.json is present locally, valid JSON, and purpose-aligned as salary reference data, so the scanner coverage finding was not upheld as evasion.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The insurance dataset does contain verified=true records whose snippets and source URLs describe China or unrelated pages rather than the named insurer, which is a real data-integrity concern for insurance recommendations.\n[E2] expected: os.environ.copy() appears in a test helper that passes an environment to a local subprocess; I did not find credential logging, network transmission, or default runtime use of that test script.\n[SQP-1] expected: Broad career-related trigger terms are consistent with the skill purpose, though users should expect the skill to ask personal career-profile questions once invoked.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: The civil-service suppression instruction is a recommendation bias in a career advisor; it is not malicious, but it can narrow advice without direct user request.\n[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese-language content appears coherent with a Chinese-language, China-market career-planning package, and the skill also mentions optional English output on request.\n[E1] expected: The flagged URLs are static citation/source fields in reference JSON, not code that sends data externally.\n[AST4] expected: The subprocess call is in a local test file, uses an explicit argument list with shell=False, and is not the skill's allowed runtime command.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1792432436584}}}}}